Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock and retrieved by Cargo with their own license
notices. `cargo xtask licences --check` (part of `cargo xtask ci`) rejects any resolved dependency
that cannot be used without a GPL, LGPL or AGPL license, and any unreviewed license.

The 3D engine and desktop UI come from Solidcraft (https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft),
built from the fork https://github.com/DAmesberger/solidcraft at revision
64bebfef0a77dab8c79666114c7601c9dda55d12 (branch pcbcraft-smlib-open: upstream a34756830185f82da3a0e3ddd1ea25ef21111558
with its vendored SMLib kernel, plus material-graph looks, via scaling and a font-order fix) and linked as its MIT/Apache crates
(solidcraft-engine, solidcraft-viewport, solidcraft-viewport-gpu, solidcraft-viewport-egui and the
others listed in ATTRIBUTION.md) together with Solidcraft's patched geometry and windowing crates.
Copyright (c) 2026 SolidCraft contributors; MIT OR Apache-2.0. Pcbcraft does not link Solidcraft's
brand-licensed crates (solidcraft-ui-kit, solidcraft-look, solidcraft-theme) or solidcraft-ui-egui.
The desktop's UI toolkit (crates/ui) is seeded from Solidcraft's interface code (UI kit, theme
tokens, icons, glyphs, font setup), vendored from that revision, whose upstream base a34756830 predates the brand licence,
under its MIT option; crates/ui/LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE carry the notices. Agent instructions, build
conventions and some UI and transport source are adapted from the same revision under its MIT
option; ATTRIBUTION.md lists the files and licenses/solidcraft-MIT.txt preserves the notice.
The fork's renderer contains Apache-2.0 code adapted from the Khronos PBR Neutral tone mapper
(Copyright The Khronos Group Inc.); the fork's NOTICE carries that attribution and applies to the
built renderer.

Expression scripting embeds Rhai 1.27.0 (https://github.com/rhaiscript/rhai), MIT OR Apache-2.0,
used as a library.

The datasheet assistant (crates/assist) reaches the Claude API over HTTPS with ureq and rustls
(MIT OR Apache-2.0; ring: Apache-2.0 AND ISC). Its trusted root certificates come from
webpki-roots, whose certificate data is licensed under the Community Data License Agreement –
Permissive 2.0; the agreement text is in licenses/webpki-roots-CDLA-Permissive-2.0.txt.

IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono are bundled in crates/ui/assets/fonts and licensed under
the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the notices are beside each font and in licenses/ibm-plex-sans-OFL.txt
and licenses/ibm-plex-mono-OFL.txt. Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp., Reserved Font Name "Plex".

